So... is there somebody else thinking that way or are we just an exception in the grand scale of people who are willing to buy a card of this class?

 @PeterNjeim  Well, I understand your point of view, however, the names always meant the order in the stack. Even on the AMD side the names are similar for that same reason, although not exactly the same.

That being said, if you notice they keep removing the low tiers, and keep making the higher ones more expensive. So at this rate there won't be anything under xx60, and by your logic it will become low end. The kicker being that a few years back low end was less than $150, maybe even $100, while now it is $400+, which is kind of insane.  This is what companies want to push on consumes who are willing to accept it. 

Samsung and Apple have been doing the same, the galaxy S5 which came out in 2014 was $650 outright, the S10+ in 2019 merely 5 years after was $1130. They doubled the price of their flagships in 5 years, which is insane. AMD and Nvidia are doing the same thing, and tech companies in general would all love to be able to do that. Because consumers are dumb and willing to accept it doesn't make it right or justifiable at all.

